    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d553">

                <pb facs="0756" n="662" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg662"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Taylor.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-01-27"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your cable, 26th, received. Press demands in mine of 22d with all reasonable
                    discretion, of course. Nevertheless, rights and liberty of American citizens are
                    paramount objects of care of this Government. Spain’s action or proposed action
                    for her own best interests in the way of reforms in Cuba should not be allowed
                    to prolong imprisonment of American citizens.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
